      "id": "lem-corner-adapted-strong-approximations-remain-in-the-same-orthant",
      "location": "Proof 2.1",
      "defect": "missing-hypothesis",
      "evidence": "Proof 2.1 says, “On the compact remainder outside their neighbourhoods, the continuous positive ratio ... has a positive minimum by [F2].” But [F2] only licenses this for “a nonempty compact set.” The neighborhoods could cover the simplex, leaving an empty remainder, so that minimum is not then available. The local bounds already suffice in that case; the proof can handle it by omitting the remainder bound or choosing the neighborhoods to leave a point outside.",
